WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.102 --> 00:00:11.611
♪ ♪

00:00:11.613 --> 00:00:11.771
♪ ♪

00:00:11.772 --> 00:00:12.572
&gt;&gt; Chris: ON THIS FINAL

00:00:12.573 --> 00:00:12.988
WEEKEND OF CAMPAIGNING,

00:00:13.023 --> 00:00:14.506
JOE BIDEN LEFT HIS HOME BASE OF

00:00:14.540 --> 00:00:15.584
DELAWARE FOR STOPS IN MUST-WIN

00:00:15.619 --> 00:00:16.997
PENNSYLVANIA AND UPPER MIDWEST

00:00:17.031 --> 00:00:18.118
SWING STATES.

00:00:18.152 --> 00:00:20.787
JOINING US NOW FROM MINNEAPOLIS,

00:00:20.788 --> 00:00:22.188
SENATOR AMY KLOBUCHAR, A KEY

00:00:22.223 --> 00:00:23.098
SUPPORTER OF THE VICE PRESIDENT.

00:00:23.099 --> 00:00:24.783
SENATOR, A LOT OF PEOPLE WERE

00:00:24.784 --> 00:00:27.699
SURPRISED ON FRIDAY TO SEE NOT

00:00:27.734 --> 00:00:29.898
JUST PRESIDENT TRUMP, BUT FORMER

00:00:29.932 --> 00:00:31.348
VICE PRESIDENT BIDEN IN THE

00:00:31.350 --> 00:00:33.432
STATE OF MINNESOTA, A STATE THAT

00:00:33.433 --> 00:00:36.503
HASN’T VOTED FOR A REPUBLICAN

00:00:36.504 --> 00:00:38.162
FOR PRESIDENT IN 11 STRAIGHT

00:00:38.196 --> 00:00:40.074
ELECTIONS, SINCE RICHARD NIXON

00:00:40.108 --> 00:00:42.353
BACK IN 1972, BUT THERE’S A

00:00:42.387 --> 00:00:42.775
REASON.

00:00:42.777 --> 00:00:44.778
LET’S LOOK AT THE LATEST REAL

00:00:44.812 --> 00:00:45.842
CLEAR POLITICS AVERAGE OF RECENT

00:00:45.844 --> 00:00:46.821
POLLS.

00:00:46.855 --> 00:00:49.997
BIDEN LEADS THE PRESIDENT IN

00:00:50.031 --> 00:00:52.336
MINNESOTA 48% TO 43.3%, PRETTY

00:00:52.338 --> 00:00:54.901
CLOSE, SO THE QUESTION IS, ARE

00:00:54.902 --> 00:00:57.346
MINNESOTA’S TEN ELECTORAL VOTES

00:00:57.348 --> 00:00:58.197
IN PLAY?

00:00:58.198 --> 00:00:59.809
&gt;&gt; Senator Klobuchar: I DON’T

00:00:59.843 --> 00:01:01.224
BELIEVE THEY ARE AND I WAS SO

00:01:01.259 --> 00:01:03.508
PLEASED THAT VICE PRESIDENT

00:01:03.542 --> 00:01:05.413
BIDEN STOPPED BY.

00:01:05.447 --> 00:01:07.369
HE WAS IN WISCONSIN, HE WAS IN

00:01:07.371 --> 00:01:09.499
IOWA, HE IS IN VIEW POINT OUT IN

00:01:09.534 --> 00:01:10.658
PENNSYLVANIA TODAY.

00:01:10.692 --> 00:01:13.222
HE’S ALL OVER THE MIDWEST.

00:01:13.224 --> 00:01:14.969
AND SERIOUSLY, CHRIS, HE IS THE

00:01:14.970 --> 00:01:17.151
HEAD OF MINNESOTA IN MANY OTHER

00:01:17.152 --> 00:01:18.920
POLLS BY DOUBLE DIGITS.

00:01:18.921 --> 00:01:20.483
HE’S AHEAD IN WISCONSIN, WHERE I

00:01:20.518 --> 00:01:22.104
AM GOING TODAY, BRAVELY GOING AS

00:01:22.139 --> 00:01:26.280
A VIKINGS FAN TO GREEN BAY TO

00:01:26.281 --> 00:01:28.207
MEET UP WITH TAMMY BALDWIN, THE

00:01:28.208 --> 00:01:29.472
SENATOR FROM WISCONSIN.

00:01:29.473 --> 00:01:31.416
HE IS AHEAD IN SO MANY STATES IN

00:01:31.417 --> 00:01:32.331
THE MIDWEST.

00:01:32.332 --> 00:01:32.634
WHY?

00:01:32.636 --> 00:01:33.839
ONE, HE IS LEADING WITH

00:01:33.840 --> 00:01:36.546
MANUFACTURING AND A BIG WAY AND

00:01:36.547 --> 00:01:37.053
BUYING AMERICA.

00:01:37.087 --> 00:01:39.502
TWO, HE HAS BEEN WILLING TO TAKE

00:01:39.503 --> 00:01:41.458
ON THE FACT THAT WE ARE NOT TO

00:01:41.492 --> 00:01:43.237
GO SEPARATE COUNTRIES, THAT WE

00:01:43.272 --> 00:01:45.440
MUST UNITE OUR NATION AND THAT

00:01:45.473 --> 00:01:47.475
IS REALLY IMPORTANT RIGHT NOW IN

00:01:47.476 --> 00:01:48.698
THE MIDWEST STRUGGLING BIG TIME

00:01:48.699 --> 00:01:49.551
WITH THE CORONAVIRUS AND THE

00:01:49.552 --> 00:01:51.085
LAST THING I ADD, SUBURBAN

00:01:51.119 --> 00:01:52.826
VOTERS IN THE MIDWEST.

00:01:52.827 --> 00:01:54.199
AFTER YOUR DEBATE THAT YOU

00:01:54.234 --> 00:01:55.863
MODERATED WHERE HE INTERRUPTED

00:01:55.897 --> 00:01:59.000
YOU OVER 100 TIMES, HE TOOK THE

00:01:59.001 --> 00:02:00.253
STAGE AND SAID WHY DON’T

00:02:00.288 --> 00:02:01.145
SUBURBAN WOMEN LIKE ME?

00:02:01.146 --> 00:02:02.720
WELL, I CAN TELL YOU SOMEONE

00:02:02.754 --> 00:02:05.035
THAT GREW UP IN THE SUBURBS,

00:02:05.070 --> 00:02:06.477
THEY DON’T LIKE THE LACK OF

00:02:06.478 --> 00:02:07.440
CIVILITY.

00:02:07.441 --> 00:02:10.635
&gt;&gt; Chris: I ASKED COREY ABOUT

00:02:10.636 --> 00:02:12.517
VOTER SUPPRESSION BUT I WANT TO

00:02:12.552 --> 00:02:15.580
TAKE A LOOK AT A CASE IN

00:02:15.582 --> 00:02:18.194
MINNESOTA WHERE TRADITIONALLY

00:02:18.229 --> 00:02:20.704
VOTES HAVE TO BE IN, RECEIVED,

00:02:20.705 --> 00:02:23.043
BY THE ELECTION BOARD BEFORE THE

00:02:23.044 --> 00:02:24.901
END OF ELECTION NIGHT TO BE

00:02:24.935 --> 00:02:27.985
COUNTED, BUT THE STATE THIS YEAR

00:02:28.019 --> 00:02:30.229
MADE A CHANGE AND SAID THAT IF

00:02:30.230 --> 00:02:32.002
VOTES ARE POSTMARKED BY ELECTION

00:02:32.004 --> 00:02:34.636
DAY, THEY CAN COME IN AS MUCH AS

00:02:34.637 --> 00:02:36.659
SEVEN DAYS LATER AND STILL BE

00:02:36.693 --> 00:02:39.043
COUNTED, SO BY A TWO TO ONE

00:02:39.077 --> 00:02:40.180
VOTE, A FEDERAL APPEALS COURT

00:02:40.214 --> 00:02:41.685
SAID THOSE VOTES THAT DON’T COME

00:02:41.686 --> 00:02:43.734
IN BY ELECTION DAY ARE GOING TO

00:02:43.735 --> 00:02:44.942
BE SEPARATED AND KEPT SEPARATE

00:02:44.943 --> 00:02:46.804
UNTIL A COURT CAN ROLL WHETHER

00:02:46.839 --> 00:02:48.390
THEY SHOULD BE COUNTED OR NOT.

00:02:48.391 --> 00:02:49.272
THAT’S A PRETTY DRAMATIC CHANGE

00:02:49.274 --> 00:02:51.300
IN THE RULES.

00:02:51.334 --> 00:02:52.809
ISN’T THAT A LEGITIMATE

00:02:52.810 --> 00:02:53.718
CHALLENGE THE REPUBLICANS?

00:02:53.719 --> 00:02:55.090
&gt;&gt; Senator Klobuchar: FIRST OF

00:02:55.092 --> 00:02:56.677
ALL, CHRIS, THE REPUBLICANS AND

00:02:56.711 --> 00:03:00.081
THE TRUMP CAMPAIGN ACTUALLY

00:03:00.115 --> 00:03:02.159
AGREED TO [INDISCERNIBLE] SO

00:03:02.194 --> 00:03:04.788
THEY COULD BE POSTMARKED BY THE

00:03:04.789 --> 00:03:05.850
ELECTION BECAUSE OF THE

00:03:05.885 --> 00:03:06.730
PANDEMIC.

00:03:06.731 --> 00:03:08.367
TWO ELECTORS WENT AROUND

00:03:08.368 --> 00:03:10.666
REPUBLICAN ELECTORS AND WENT TO

00:03:10.700 --> 00:03:11.517
THE COURTS.

00:03:11.551 --> 00:03:13.192
WE REALLY ARE FOCUSED RIGHT NOW

00:03:13.226 --> 00:03:15.184
ON MAKING SURE PEOPLE CAN VOTE

00:03:15.185 --> 00:03:16.794
AND WE ARE JUST TELLING THEM

00:03:16.795 --> 00:03:18.862
DON’T VOTE BY MAIL ANYMORE, TAKE

00:03:18.863 --> 00:03:20.220
YOUR BALLOT TO A DROP OFF BOX.

00:03:20.221 --> 00:03:22.115
WE’VE GOT PLENTY OF THEM IN

00:03:22.116 --> 00:03:23.620
MINNESOTA, IT’S NOT LIKE TEXAS

00:03:23.621 --> 00:03:25.475
WHERE PEOPLE ARE STILL VALIANTLY

00:03:25.509 --> 00:03:26.829
PHONING THAT ONLY HAVE ONE PER

00:03:26.863 --> 00:03:27.199
COUNTY.

00:03:27.233 --> 00:03:28.740
AND THEN SHOW UP IN PERSON.

00:03:28.741 --> 00:03:30.845
WE HAVE EARLY VOTING GOING ON

00:03:30.879 --> 00:03:32.137
ALL DAY TODAY, TOMORROW,

00:03:32.138 --> 00:03:33.901
ELECTION DAY, SO WE STILL FEEL

00:03:33.902 --> 00:03:35.577
REALLY GOOD ABOUT THE VOTING IN

00:03:35.578 --> 00:03:35.920
MINNESOTA.

00:03:35.921 --> 00:03:38.721
WE ARE NUMBER ONE IN THE COUNTRY

00:03:38.722 --> 00:03:39.412
NEARLY EVERY PRESIDENTIAL

00:03:39.413 --> 00:03:41.347
ELECTION VOTING, SO WE ARE

00:03:41.381 --> 00:03:42.848
POSITIVE ABOUT IT AND IT IS AN

00:03:42.883 --> 00:03:44.595
EXAMPLE OF THE KIND OF ATTEMPTS

00:03:44.596 --> 00:03:47.337
WE ARE SEEING TO CUT PEOPLE OUT

00:03:47.338 --> 00:03:47.817
FROM VOTING.

00:03:47.818 --> 00:03:48.464
I THINK IT’S WRONG.

00:03:48.465 --> 00:03:49.837
&gt;&gt; Chris: I WANT TO TALK TO

00:03:49.838 --> 00:03:52.112
ABOUT SOME ISSUES.

00:03:52.146 --> 00:03:54.009
IN THE FINAL PRESIDENTIAL DEBATE

00:03:54.010 --> 00:03:56.463
JOE BIDEN SAID THAT HE WOULD --

00:03:56.464 --> 00:03:58.470
THESE ARE HIS WORDS --

00:03:58.505 --> 00:04:00.508
TRANSITION FROM THE OIL INDUSTRY

00:04:00.509 --> 00:04:01.748
AND DURING THE DEMOCRATIC

00:04:01.783 --> 00:04:03.961
PRIMARY DEBATES, WHEN YOU WERE

00:04:03.962 --> 00:04:04.807
RUNNING AGAINST JOE BIDEN,

00:04:04.808 --> 00:04:06.873
DURING ONE OF THEM HE SAID HE

00:04:06.907 --> 00:04:07.742
WOULD ELIMINATE FRACKING.

00:04:07.743 --> 00:04:10.108
HE’S KIND OF TRIED TO PULL BACK

00:04:10.109 --> 00:04:12.250
FROM BOTH OF THOSE STATEMENTS.

00:04:12.251 --> 00:04:13.376
HERE’S WHAT THE PRESIDENT SAID

00:04:13.410 --> 00:04:15.678
THIS WEEK ABOUT JOE BIDEN.

00:04:15.679 --> 00:04:17.889
&gt;&gt; JOE BIDEN CONFIRMED HIS PLAN

00:04:17.923 --> 00:04:19.248
TO ABOLISH THE ENTIRE U.S. OIL

00:04:19.282 --> 00:04:19.666
INDUSTRY.

00:04:19.701 --> 00:04:21.408
I SAID YOU MEAN NO MORE OIL,

00:04:21.409 --> 00:04:22.606
JOE?

00:04:22.640 --> 00:04:26.128
THAT’S WHAT I MEAN.

00:04:26.130 --> 00:04:29.383
&gt;&gt; Chris: BIDEN SAYS HE WANTS

00:04:29.417 --> 00:04:31.376
ZERO NET EMISSIONS OF GREENHOUSE

00:04:31.411 --> 00:04:32.275
GASES BY 2050.

00:04:32.277 --> 00:04:33.743
FACT IS, IF YOU’RE GOING TO

00:04:33.744 --> 00:04:34.920
REALLY DO ALL THOSE THINGS THAT

00:04:34.955 --> 00:04:36.479
HE’S TALKING ABOUT, IT’S GOING

00:04:36.480 --> 00:04:39.562
TO HURT A LOT OF PEOPLE WHO

00:04:39.563 --> 00:04:41.128
DEPEND ON FOSSIL FUELS FOR JOBS.

00:04:41.129 --> 00:04:42.284
&gt;&gt; Senator Klobuchar: WELL,

00:04:42.286 --> 00:04:43.314
LET ME CLARIFY THE FACTS, FIRST

00:04:43.315 --> 00:04:44.395
OF ALL.

00:04:44.397 --> 00:04:46.691
HE HAS MADE VERY CLEAR THAT HE

00:04:46.726 --> 00:04:49.248
IS NOT AGAINST FRACKING, HE JUST

00:04:49.282 --> 00:04:50.678
WANTS TO HAVE SAFETY RULES IN

00:04:50.679 --> 00:04:53.181
PLACE AND NATURAL GAS --

00:04:53.216 --> 00:04:55.040
&gt;&gt; Chris: NO NO.

00:04:55.074 --> 00:04:56.962
I MEAN AGAIN -- SENATOR, LET ME

00:04:56.997 --> 00:04:57.275
FACT-CHECK.

00:04:57.276 --> 00:04:58.097
&gt;&gt; Senator Klobuchar: OKAY.

00:04:58.099 --> 00:04:58.387
OKAY.

00:04:58.389 --> 00:04:59.725
&gt;&gt; Chris: HE SAID HE WILL NOT

00:04:59.726 --> 00:05:01.429
ALLOW ANY NEW FRACKING ON

00:05:01.464 --> 00:05:02.584
FEDERAL LANDS.

00:05:02.586 --> 00:05:04.613
&gt;&gt; Senator Klobuchar: OKAY,

00:05:04.615 --> 00:05:05.359
THAT IS CORRECT.

00:05:05.393 --> 00:05:06.465
WE ARE TALKING BUT EXISTING

00:05:06.499 --> 00:05:07.013
FRACKING.

00:05:07.048 --> 00:05:08.653
SECONDLY, WHAT HE’S TALKING

00:05:08.688 --> 00:05:10.911
ABOUT IS STOPPING THESE OIL

00:05:10.945 --> 00:05:11.919
SUBSIDIES AND TRANSITIONING TO

00:05:11.953 --> 00:05:14.207
RENEWABLE FUELS TO BRING DOWN

00:05:14.208 --> 00:05:14.979
GREENHOUSE GAS EMISSIONS.

00:05:15.014 --> 00:05:17.449
LOOK AT THE FIRES RAGING IN THE

00:05:17.483 --> 00:05:18.963
WEST COAST, OUR MILITARY

00:05:18.964 --> 00:05:20.526
PREDICTED THIS, CHRIS, THAT THIS

00:05:20.560 --> 00:05:21.668
WOULD HAPPEN, AND THAT’S WHAT

00:05:21.669 --> 00:05:22.445
HAPPENED THIS PAST FALL.

00:05:22.446 --> 00:05:24.028
YOU LOOK AT ALL THE FLOODING WE

00:05:24.063 --> 00:05:25.395
ARE SEEING, THE WEIRD WEATHER

00:05:25.396 --> 00:05:26.832
EVENTS, THE INCREASE IN

00:05:26.833 --> 00:05:28.459
HURRICANES, THE EFFECT THAT IT

00:05:28.461 --> 00:05:29.908
HAS HAD ON THE STATE OF FLORIDA.

00:05:29.910 --> 00:05:31.947
THEY ARE STILL COMING IN AND I

00:05:31.982 --> 00:05:34.199
THINK THAT WHAT HE IS TALKING

00:05:34.200 --> 00:05:36.141
ABOUT IS SHARED BY SCIENTISTS

00:05:36.176 --> 00:05:37.474
AND BY ACTUALLY OUR OWN MILITARY

00:05:37.508 --> 00:05:38.586
THAT WE NEED TO START TACKLING

00:05:38.587 --> 00:05:40.901
THIS PROBLEM AND HE’S GOING TO

00:05:40.903 --> 00:05:43.095
DO IT IN A SMART WAY THAT WILL

00:05:43.129 --> 00:05:44.661
EVENTUALLY ADD MORE JOBS TO

00:05:44.662 --> 00:05:44.914
AMERICA.

00:05:44.915 --> 00:05:46.824
I THINK THAT’S WHAT’S IMPORTANT

00:05:46.825 --> 00:05:48.686
BUT I DID WANT TO GET AT SOME

00:05:48.687 --> 00:05:49.396
THE ECONOMIC ARGUMENTS THAT

00:05:49.430 --> 00:05:51.165
COREY WAS MAKING IN HIS SEGMENT

00:05:51.166 --> 00:05:51.979
BEFORE I WENT ON.

00:05:52.014 --> 00:05:53.466
I THOUGHT IT WAS FASCINATING

00:05:53.467 --> 00:05:54.445
FROM FOX.

00:05:54.446 --> 00:05:56.291
SPIRIT I’VE GOT -- YOU KNOW --

00:05:56.325 --> 00:05:56.721
THANK YOU.

00:05:56.723 --> 00:05:58.672
&gt;&gt; Senator Klobuchar: YOU ARE

00:05:58.673 --> 00:05:59.200
THE MODERATOR.

00:05:59.235 --> 00:06:01.275
&gt;&gt; Chris: THANK YOU.

00:06:01.277 --> 00:06:01.954
[LAUGHS]

00:06:01.988 --> 00:06:02.727
THANK YOU!

00:06:02.761 --> 00:06:04.076
I SOMETIMES FORGET THAT.

00:06:04.077 --> 00:06:05.081
BEYOND THE PRESIDENTIAL RACE,

00:06:05.082 --> 00:06:06.329
THE OTHER BIG ELECTION NEWS OF

00:06:06.364 --> 00:06:08.176
COURSE IS THE RACE FOR CONTROL

00:06:08.211 --> 00:06:09.699
OF THE SENATE.

00:06:09.700 --> 00:06:13.786
THE CURRENT MARGIN 53-47, YOU

00:06:13.787 --> 00:06:16.512
NEED A NET PICKUP OF 4 TO

00:06:16.513 --> 00:06:19.026
CONTROL THE SENATE OR BIDEN WIN

00:06:19.027 --> 00:06:20.494
AND PICK UP OF THREE THEN

00:06:20.496 --> 00:06:21.968
VICE PRESIDENT KAMALA HARRIS

00:06:22.002 --> 00:06:23.914
WOULD BE ABLE TO BREAK THE TIE

00:06:23.949 --> 00:06:24.293
VOTE.

00:06:24.294 --> 00:06:26.069
YOU HAVE A CLOSE RACE.

00:06:26.070 --> 00:06:27.605
YOU ARE NOT IN IT BUT A CLOSE

00:06:27.639 --> 00:06:29.461
RACE IN MINNESOTA, PUT IT UP ON

00:06:29.495 --> 00:06:30.394
THE SCREEN.

00:06:30.429 --> 00:06:32.070
IT REAL CLEAR POLITICS RANKS THE

00:06:32.105 --> 00:06:34.633
MINNESOTA RACE BETWEEN THE

00:06:34.634 --> 00:06:35.416
INCUMBENT DEMOCRATIC

00:06:35.417 --> 00:06:36.996
SENATOR TINA SMITH AND

00:06:37.030 --> 00:06:37.679
REPUBLICAN CONGRESSMAN JASON

00:06:37.713 --> 00:06:39.738
LEWIS AS A TOSS-UP.

00:06:39.739 --> 00:06:41.447
QUICKLY, WHAT ARE THE CHANCES

00:06:41.448 --> 00:06:43.287
THAT SMITH WILL WIN, HOLD ONTO

00:06:43.288 --> 00:06:46.457
THAT SEAT, AND WHAT ARE THE

00:06:46.458 --> 00:06:48.160
CHANCES THE DEMOCRATS WILL TAKE

00:06:48.162 --> 00:06:49.403
OVER CONTROL OF THE SENATE?

00:06:49.437 --> 00:06:50.440
&gt;&gt; Senator Klobuchar: SMITH

00:06:50.474 --> 00:06:52.162
HOLDING ONTO A SEAT, I PUT IT

00:06:52.163 --> 00:06:52.425
100%.

00:06:52.460 --> 00:06:56.249
PAUL CAME OUT TODAY, SHE’S NINE

00:06:56.284 --> 00:06:57.045
POINTS AHEAD.

00:06:57.046 --> 00:06:59.420
SENATE RACES, WE ARE AHEAD IN

00:06:59.455 --> 00:07:01.333
ARIZONA, WE ARE AHEAD IN

00:07:01.334 --> 00:07:01.806
COLORADO.

00:07:01.841 --> 00:07:04.707
WE ARE AHEAD IN THE NUMBER OF

00:07:04.742 --> 00:07:07.042
POLLS IN MAINE.

00:07:07.076 --> 00:07:09.670
WE ARE AHEAD -- THE HOLES GO

00:07:09.705 --> 00:07:10.987
BACK AND FORTH.

00:07:11.021 --> 00:07:12.546
IN NORTH CAROLINA WE ARE AHEAD.

00:07:12.547 --> 00:07:15.100
WE ARE DOING WELL IN STATES LIKE

00:07:15.135 --> 00:07:16.147
GEORGIA, SOUTH CAROLINA, ALASKA.

00:07:16.148 --> 00:07:16.975
YOU NAME IT.

00:07:16.976 --> 00:07:18.171
IF SO I AM FEELING GOOD ABOUT

00:07:18.172 --> 00:07:19.179
THE SENATE.

00:07:19.181 --> 00:07:21.107
I CAN’T GIVE YOU A PERCENTAGE ON

00:07:21.108 --> 00:07:21.315
THAT.

00:07:21.317 --> 00:07:23.092
BUT REMEMBER, I JUST WANT TO SAY

00:07:23.127 --> 00:07:25.102
TO YOUR VIEWERS HERE, IF YOU ARE

00:07:25.103 --> 00:07:26.312
SICK AND TIRED OF A PRESIDENT

00:07:26.313 --> 00:07:28.360
THAT HAS NOT DONE WHAT HE HAS

00:07:28.395 --> 00:07:31.358
SAID HE’S DONE, WHICH IS NOT

00:07:31.359 --> 00:07:33.240
KEEP AMERICANS SAFE WHEN WE HAVE

00:07:33.274 --> 00:07:34.664
CORONAVIRUS SPIKING, PICK A GUY

00:07:34.665 --> 00:07:35.772
THAT’S GOT A PLAN, THAT’S

00:07:35.774 --> 00:07:37.620
LISTENING TO THE SCIENCE, WHO’S

00:07:37.621 --> 00:07:38.713
GOING TO DO SOMETHING ABOUT IT

00:07:38.747 --> 00:07:41.199
AND GET THE VACCINE OUT IN A WAY

00:07:41.200 --> 00:07:41.966
THAT MAKES SENSE.

00:07:42.000 --> 00:07:43.811
THIS IS REALLY THE HEART AND

00:07:43.813 --> 00:07:45.234
SOUL OF THE ARGUMENT HERE AT THE

00:07:45.235 --> 00:07:45.835
END.

00:07:45.836 --> 00:07:47.233
&gt;&gt; Chris: FINALLY, SENATOR, AS

00:07:47.234 --> 00:07:50.500
YOU SAID, I’M THE MODERATOR OR

00:07:50.535 --> 00:07:52.653
IN THIS CASE THE HOST.

00:07:52.687 --> 00:07:57.062
SENATOR, JOE BIDEN AND YOU RAN

00:07:57.063 --> 00:07:59.395
IN THE CENTRIST LANES DURING THE

00:07:59.430 --> 00:08:00.551
PRIMARIES, BUT IT’S BEEN

00:08:00.552 --> 00:08:01.552
INTERESTING WATCHING WHAT’S

00:08:01.587 --> 00:08:02.777
HAPPENING IN THE LAST FEW DAYS.

00:08:02.811 --> 00:08:04.973
ELIZABETH WARREN IS SAYING SHE

00:08:04.974 --> 00:08:07.446
WOULD LIKE TO BE SECRETARY OF

00:08:07.481 --> 00:08:08.000
THE TREASURY.

00:08:08.034 --> 00:08:09.552
BERNIE SANDERS HAS TALKED ABOUT

00:08:09.586 --> 00:08:11.437
PUSHING FOR SECRETARY OF LABOR.

00:08:11.438 --> 00:08:12.799
KAMALA HARRIS, WHO WOULD BE

00:08:12.834 --> 00:08:14.065
VICE PRESIDENT, IS RATED THE

00:08:14.067 --> 00:08:14.945
MOST LIBERAL MEMBER OF THE

00:08:14.979 --> 00:08:15.834
SENATE.

00:08:15.835 --> 00:08:19.526
IF JOE BIDEN WINS, ISN’T THE

00:08:19.527 --> 00:08:22.407
LEFT GOING TO COME AFTER HIM

00:08:22.408 --> 00:08:24.552
REALLY HARD AFTER THE ELECTION?

00:08:24.553 --> 00:08:25.428
&gt;&gt; Senator Klobuchar: CHRIS,

00:08:25.462 --> 00:08:27.329
RIGHT NOW JOE BIDEN IS FOCUSED

00:08:27.363 --> 00:08:28.730
ON UNITING THIS COUNTRY AND OUR

00:08:28.764 --> 00:08:30.304
PARTY HAD STAYED UNITED, BUT

00:08:30.339 --> 00:08:32.057
WHAT I THINK IS REALLY IMPORTANT

00:08:32.058 --> 00:08:33.926
TO REALIZE, HE HAS BROUGHT AND

00:08:33.960 --> 00:08:35.755
PEOPLE LIKE JOHN KASICH, FORMER

00:08:35.790 --> 00:08:36.943
GOVERNOR, REPUBLICAN GOVERNOR OF

00:08:36.945 --> 00:08:37.155
OHIO.

00:08:37.189 --> 00:08:37.989
CINDY McCAIN --

00:08:37.990 --> 00:08:39.473
&gt;&gt; Chris: BUT HE’S NOT GOING

00:08:39.507 --> 00:08:40.957
TO BE IN THE CABINET.

00:08:40.958 --> 00:08:41.585
I’M TALKING ABOUT

00:08:41.619 --> 00:08:42.780
ELIZABETH WARREN AS TREASURY

00:08:42.782 --> 00:08:44.042
SECRETARY OR BERNIE SANDERS AS

00:08:44.077 --> 00:08:44.633
LABOR SECRETARY.

00:08:44.634 --> 00:08:45.677
&gt;&gt; Senator Klobuchar: I HAVE

00:08:45.711 --> 00:08:47.012
NO IDEA WHO HE’S GOING TO PICK

00:08:47.046 --> 00:08:47.780
FOR THE CABINET.

00:08:47.815 --> 00:08:49.980
WHAT I DO KNOW IS THE WAY HE HAS

00:08:49.981 --> 00:08:51.022
RUN HIS CAMPAIGN, THE WAY HE HAS

00:08:51.057 --> 00:08:52.021
SAID HE’S GOING TO BE THE

00:08:52.055 --> 00:08:52.874
PRESIDENT NOT JUST FOR THE

00:08:52.908 --> 00:08:54.248
PEOPLE TO VOTE FOR HIM BUT THE

00:08:54.283 --> 00:08:55.869
PEOPLE THAT VOTE AGAINST HIM.

00:08:55.870 --> 00:08:57.794
THAT’S HOW HE’S GOING TO GOVERN.

00:08:57.828 --> 00:08:59.903
HE HAS GOT SO MUCH TO DO IN

00:08:59.905 --> 00:09:01.333
THOSE FIRST 100 DAYS AND I JUST

00:09:01.335 --> 00:09:02.593
THINK THAT THIS ELECTION, IF IT

00:09:02.628 --> 00:09:04.453
GOES DOWN THE WAY WE ARE SEEING

00:09:04.454 --> 00:09:06.652
WITH HIM AHEAD IN PLACES LIKE

00:09:06.654 --> 00:09:08.316
GEORGIA AND SOME POLLS IN TEXAS,

00:09:08.351 --> 00:09:10.933
THIS IS GOING TO BE THE COUNTRY

00:09:10.935 --> 00:09:12.022
SAYING "ENOUGH OF THE DIVIDE.

00:09:12.023 --> 00:09:13.321
ENOUGH OF THE FIGHTING.

00:09:13.323 --> 00:09:14.663
WE WANT TO GO TOGETHER AS A

00:09:14.664 --> 00:09:15.139
TEAM.

00:09:15.140 --> 00:09:17.454
TEAM AMERICA AND MOVE FORWARD

00:09:17.488 --> 00:09:19.203
AND WIN THIS THING FOR OUR

00:09:19.237 --> 00:09:20.742
COUNTRY" AND THAT MEANS TAKING

00:09:20.777 --> 00:09:22.525
ON THIS VIRUS, SHUTTING DOWN A

00:09:22.526 --> 00:09:23.625
VIRUS, AND OPENING UP OUR

00:09:23.659 --> 00:09:24.433
ECONOMY.

00:09:24.434 --> 00:09:25.904
THAT’S WHAT THIS IS ABOUT.

